1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,779
Welcome to Unit Nine of Algebra One:
quadratic functions and equations.

2
00:00:05,229 --> 00:00:08,578
In this lesson, we'll look at the graphs
of quadratic functions.

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:16,090
A quadratic function has the form f of x
equals a x squared plus b x plus c, with a

4
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:16,783
not zero.

5
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:22,607
The simplest one is y equals x squared.
Its graph is a U-shaped curve called a

6
00:00:22,607 --> 00:00:23,227
parabola.

7
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:29,599
The turning point of a parabola is the
vertex. For y equals x squared, it's the

8
00:00:29,599 --> 00:00:30,063
origin.

9
00:00:30,513 --> 00:00:35,489
The parabola is symmetric about a vertical
line through the vertex, called the axis

10
00:00:35,489 --> 00:00:36,209
of symmetry.

11
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:41,515
When a is positive, the parabola opens up,
and the vertex is a minimum.

12
00:00:41,965 --> 00:00:47,169
When a is negative, it opens down, and the
vertex is a maximum. The bigger the size

13
00:00:47,169 --> 00:00:49,175
of a, the narrower the parabola.

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:54,247
The axis of symmetry is x equals negative
b over two a.

15
00:00:54,697 --> 00:01:00,294
For y equals x squared minus four x plus
three, that's four over two, which is two.

16
00:01:00,294 --> 00:01:05,554
Plug in two: four minus eight plus three
is negative one. So the vertex is two

17
00:01:05,554 --> 00:01:06,835
comma negative one.

18
00:01:07,967 --> 00:01:12,340
Now graph it. Plot the vertex, then the y
intercept, zero comma three.

19
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:17,683
By symmetry, four comma three is also on
the graph. Connect them with a smooth

20
00:01:17,683 --> 00:01:18,059
curve.

21
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:24,235
Your turn. Find the vertex of y equals x
squared plus six x plus five.

22
00:01:24,685 --> 00:01:26,135
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:26,585 --> 00:01:31,922
x equals negative six over two, which is
negative three. Then y is nine minus

24
00:01:31,922 --> 00:01:37,327
eighteen plus five, which is negative
four. The vertex is negative three comma

25
00:01:37,327 --> 00:01:38,297
negative four.

26
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:43,742
Let's find the key features of a quadratic
in standard form and sketch it.

27
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:50,963
For f of x equals x squared minus six x
plus five, find the direction, the axis of

28
00:01:50,963 --> 00:01:54,638
symmetry, the vertex, the y intercept and
the range.

29
00:01:55,766 --> 00:02:00,304
a is one, which is positive, so the
parabola opens up and the vertex is a

30
00:02:00,304 --> 00:02:00,801
minimum.

31
00:02:01,933 --> 00:02:07,792
The axis of symmetry is x equals negative
b over two a, which is six over two, or

32
00:02:07,792 --> 00:02:08,226
three.

33
00:02:09,366 --> 00:02:14,548
Plug in three: nine minus eighteen plus
five is negative four. The vertex is

34
00:02:14,548 --> 00:02:15,980
three, negative four.

35
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,809
The y intercept is f of zero, which is
five.

36
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:25,690
Since the minimum is negative four, the
range is y at least negative four.

37
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:32,647
It opens up, with axis x equals three,
vertex three, negative four, y intercept

38
00:02:32,647 --> 00:02:35,665
five, and range y at least negative four.

39
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:42,060
Watch out. In negative b over two a, be
careful with the sign of b. a positive

40
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:47,253
opens up, a negative opens down. And use
symmetry to get a free second point.

41
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:54,135
Your turn. Find the vertex of g of x
equals negative two x squared plus eight x

42
00:02:54,135 --> 00:02:57,040
minus three. Pause the video and try it.

43
00:03:01,566 --> 00:03:07,251
x equals negative eight over negative
four, which is two. g of two is five. The

44
00:03:07,251 --> 00:03:09,481
vertex is two, five, a maximum.

45
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:15,566
In this lesson, we'll write parabolas in
vertex form, which shows the vertex right

46
00:03:15,566 --> 00:03:15,869
away.

47
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:22,355
Vertex form is y equals a times the
quantity x minus h, squared, plus k.

48
00:03:22,805 --> 00:03:24,469
The vertex is h comma k.

49
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:27,605
The h shifts the graph left or right.

50
00:03:28,055 --> 00:03:33,786
y equals x minus three, squared, moves y
equals x squared three units right. Watch

51
00:03:33,786 --> 00:03:36,162
the sign: minus three means right.

52
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,199
The k shifts the graph up or down.

53
00:03:39,649 --> 00:03:42,486
y equals x squared plus two moves it up
two.

54
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:45,297
The a stretches or reflects it.

55
00:03:45,747 --> 00:03:51,526
y equals two x squared is narrower. y
equals negative x squared flips it upside

56
00:03:51,526 --> 00:03:51,891
down.

57
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:57,620
Graph y equals negative the quantity x
plus one, squared, plus four.

58
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:01,803
The vertex is negative one comma four, and
it opens down.

59
00:04:02,933 --> 00:04:08,274
Your turn. What is the vertex of y equals
two times the quantity x minus five,

60
00:04:08,274 --> 00:04:11,424
squared, minus three? Does it open up or
down?

61
00:04:11,874 --> 00:04:13,325
Pause the video and try it.

62
00:04:13,775 --> 00:04:18,063
The vertex is five comma negative three,
and since a is two, it opens up.

63
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:23,787
Here's a worked example of writing a
quadratic from its vertex and one point.

64
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:30,859
A parabola has vertex two, negative three
and passes through four, five. Write its

65
00:04:30,859 --> 00:04:34,769
equation in vertex form and describe the
transformations.

66
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:40,252
Vertex form is y equals a times x minus h,
squared, plus k.

67
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,749
Plug in the vertex: h is two and k is
negative three.

68
00:04:45,867 --> 00:04:47,979
Use the point four, five to find a.

69
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:52,876
Five equals four a minus three, so four a
is eight and a is two.

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,821
The equation is y equals two times x minus
two, squared, minus three.

71
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:05,582
The equation is y equals two times x minus
two squared, minus three. Compared to y

72
00:05:05,582 --> 00:05:10,719
equals x squared, it's stretched by two,
shifted right two, and down three.

73
00:05:11,867 --> 00:05:17,144
Watch out. x minus h with h equals two
means a shift to the right, not the left.

74
00:05:17,144 --> 00:05:22,025
You always need another point to find a.
And a larger a makes the parabola

75
00:05:22,025 --> 00:05:22,619
narrower.

76
00:05:23,767 --> 00:05:29,096
Your turn. The vertex is negative one,
four and the parabola passes through one,

77
00:05:29,096 --> 00:05:33,559
negative four. Write it in vertex form.
Pause the video and try it.

78
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:44,016
Negative four equals a times two squared
plus four, so a is negative two. y equals

79
00:05:44,016 --> 00:05:47,551
negative two times x plus one squared,
plus four.

80
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:53,655
Now we start solving quadratic equations.
In this lesson, we'll use graphs and

81
00:05:53,655 --> 00:05:54,481
square roots.

82
00:05:55,600 --> 00:06:01,535
The solutions of a x squared plus b x plus
c equals zero are the x intercepts of the

83
00:06:01,535 --> 00:06:02,171
parabola.

84
00:06:02,621 --> 00:06:08,091
They're also called roots or zeros. For y
equals x squared minus four, the graph

85
00:06:08,091 --> 00:06:10,279
crosses at negative two and two.

86
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:15,475
A parabola can cross the x axis twice,
touch it once, or miss it.

87
00:06:15,925 --> 00:06:19,829
So a quadratic equation has two, one, or
no real solutions.

88
00:06:20,967 --> 00:06:25,255
When there's no x term, use square roots.
x squared equals twenty-five.

89
00:06:25,705 --> 00:06:29,715
x can be five, or negative five. Don't
forget the negative root.

90
00:06:30,833 --> 00:06:33,991
Solve three x squared minus forty-eight
equals zero.

91
00:06:34,441 --> 00:06:39,844
Add forty-eight: three x squared equals
forty-eight. Divide by three: x squared

92
00:06:39,844 --> 00:06:43,059
equals sixteen. So x equals plus or minus
four.

93
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:47,485
Solve the quantity x minus two, squared,
equals nine.

94
00:06:47,935 --> 00:06:53,958
Take square roots: x minus two equals plus
or minus three. So x equals five, or x

95
00:06:53,958 --> 00:06:55,445
equals negative one.

96
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:59,681
Your turn. Solve two x squared equals
seventy-two.

97
00:07:00,131 --> 00:07:01,582
Pause the video and try it.

98
00:07:02,032 --> 00:07:06,171
x squared equals thirty-six, so x equals
plus or minus six.

99
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:11,481
Let's solve a quadratic by isolating the
square and taking square roots.

100
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:17,465
Solve three times x minus four squared,
minus seven, equals forty one.

101
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:24,027
Isolate the squared part. Add seven: three
times x minus four squared equals forty

102
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:24,424
eight.

103
00:07:25,567 --> 00:07:29,087
Divide by three: x minus four squared
equals sixteen.

104
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:35,706
Take the square root of both sides,
remembering plus or minus: x minus four is

105
00:07:35,706 --> 00:07:37,039
plus or minus four.

106
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,959
The plus case: x equals eight.

107
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:43,191
The minus case: x equals zero.

108
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:47,683
The solutions are x equals zero and x
equals eight.

109
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:53,773
Watch out. Isolate the squared expression
before you take the square root. Always

110
00:07:53,773 --> 00:07:58,807
include plus or minus. And if the square
equals a negative number, there's no real

111
00:07:58,807 --> 00:07:59,360
solution.

112
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:05,595
Your turn. Solve two times x plus one
squared equals fifty. Pause the video and

113
00:08:05,595 --> 00:08:06,047
try it.

114
00:08:10,567 --> 00:08:16,730
x plus one squared is twenty five, so x
plus one is plus or minus five. x is four

115
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:17,948
or negative six.

116
00:08:19,066 --> 00:08:23,913
In Unit Eight we learned to factor. In
this lesson, we'll use factoring to solve

117
00:08:23,913 --> 00:08:25,125
quadratic equations.

118
00:08:26,266 --> 00:08:31,766
The zero product property: if a times b
equals zero, then a equals zero, or b

119
00:08:31,766 --> 00:08:32,623
equals zero.

120
00:08:33,073 --> 00:08:35,207
It only works with zero on one side.

121
00:08:36,333 --> 00:08:41,602
Solve the quantity x minus three, times
the quantity x plus five, equals zero.

122
00:08:42,052 --> 00:08:48,434
Either x minus three is zero, so x equals
three, or x plus five is zero, so x equals

123
00:08:48,434 --> 00:08:49,497
negative five.

124
00:08:50,633 --> 00:08:53,918
Solve x squared plus x minus twelve equals
zero.

125
00:08:54,368 --> 00:09:00,321
Factor: x plus four, times x minus three.
So x equals negative four, or x equals

126
00:09:00,321 --> 00:09:00,768
three.

127
00:09:01,899 --> 00:09:03,969
Solve x squared equals five x.

128
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:10,613
First get zero on one side: x squared
minus five x equals zero. Factor out x: x

129
00:09:10,613 --> 00:09:13,123
times the quantity x minus five.

130
00:09:13,573 --> 00:09:19,055
So x equals zero or five. Don't divide by
x, or you'll lose the zero solution.

131
00:09:20,199 --> 00:09:23,975
Solve two x squared plus seven x plus
three equals zero.

132
00:09:24,425 --> 00:09:30,605
It factors as two x plus one, times x plus
three. So x equals negative one half, or

133
00:09:30,605 --> 00:09:31,721
negative three.

134
00:09:32,866 --> 00:09:37,154
Your turn. Solve x squared minus seven x
plus ten equals zero.

135
00:09:37,604 --> 00:09:39,055
Pause the video and try it.

136
00:09:39,505 --> 00:09:44,945
It factors as x minus two, times x minus
five. So x equals two or five.

137
00:09:45,066 --> 00:09:46,066
Next time, we'll solve by completing the
square. If this helped, subscribe to

138
00:09:46,066 --> 00:09:50,787
Here's a worked example of solving a
quadratic by factoring, starting from a

139
00:09:50,787 --> 00:09:51,719
messy equation.

140
00:09:53,166 --> 00:09:56,110
Solve two x squared plus five x equals
twelve.

141
00:09:57,233 --> 00:10:01,009
First, set the equation equal to zero by
subtracting twelve.

142
00:10:02,133 --> 00:10:07,549
Use the A C method. a c is negative twenty
four, and eight and negative three add to

143
00:10:07,549 --> 00:10:07,871
five.

144
00:10:08,999 --> 00:10:10,258
Split the middle and group.

145
00:10:11,399 --> 00:10:14,919
That's two x minus three times x plus four
equals zero.

146
00:10:16,066 --> 00:10:21,775
By the zero product property, either two x
minus three is zero, giving three halves,

147
00:10:21,775 --> 00:10:24,834
or x plus four is zero, giving negative
four.

148
00:10:25,966 --> 00:10:28,611
The solutions are three halves and
negative four.

149
00:10:29,733 --> 00:10:35,001
Watch out. Get zero on one side before
factoring; the zero product property only

150
00:10:35,001 --> 00:10:40,335
works with zero. And never divide both
sides by x, because you'd lose a solution.

151
00:10:41,466 --> 00:10:45,882
Your turn. Solve x squared equals seven x.
Pause the video and try it.

152
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:56,489
Subtract seven x and factor: x times x
minus seven equals zero. x is zero or

153
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:56,970
seven.

154
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:02,673
Not every quadratic factors nicely.
Completing the square works on any

155
00:11:02,673 --> 00:11:03,327
quadratic.

156
00:11:04,467 --> 00:11:09,501
x squared plus six x plus nine is a
perfect square: x plus three, squared.

157
00:11:09,951 --> 00:11:14,837
The nine comes from half of six, squared.
Half of b, squared, completes the square.

158
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:18,804
Here are the steps. Move the constant to
the right side.

159
00:11:19,254 --> 00:11:24,049
Add half of b, squared, to both sides.
Then write the left side as a square and

160
00:11:24,049 --> 00:11:25,142
take square roots.

161
00:11:26,267 --> 00:11:29,829
Solve x squared plus six x minus seven
equals zero.

162
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:35,664
Move the seven: x squared plus six x
equals seven. Add nine to both sides: x

163
00:11:35,664 --> 00:11:38,215
plus three, squared, equals sixteen.

164
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:45,108
So x plus three equals plus or minus four.
x equals one, or x equals negative seven.

165
00:11:46,233 --> 00:11:49,540
When b is odd, you get fractions, but the
steps are the same.

166
00:11:49,990 --> 00:11:54,844
For x squared plus three x, half of three
is three halves, and its square is nine

167
00:11:54,844 --> 00:11:55,323
fourths.

168
00:11:56,467 --> 00:11:59,176
Completing the square also gives vertex
form.

169
00:11:59,626 --> 00:12:05,473
x squared minus four x plus one equals x
minus two, squared, minus three. So the

170
00:12:05,473 --> 00:12:08,031
vertex is two comma negative three.

171
00:12:09,167 --> 00:12:14,536
Your turn. Solve x squared plus four x
minus five equals zero by completing the

172
00:12:14,536 --> 00:12:15,012
square.

173
00:12:15,462 --> 00:12:16,913
Pause the video and try it.

174
00:12:17,363 --> 00:12:23,668
x squared plus four x equals five. Add
four: x plus two, squared, equals nine. So

175
00:12:23,668 --> 00:12:26,003
x equals one or negative five.

176
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:30,589
Let's complete the square when the leading
coefficient isn't one.

177
00:12:32,233 --> 00:12:37,306
Solve two x squared minus twelve x plus
seven equals zero by completing the

178
00:12:37,306 --> 00:12:37,780
square.

179
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:42,910
First divide every term by two, so the
leading coefficient is one.

180
00:12:44,033 --> 00:12:45,868
Move the constant to the right side.

181
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,288
Take half of negative six, which is
negative three, and square it: nine.

182
00:12:52,433 --> 00:12:57,340
Add nine to both sides. Negative seven
halves plus nine is eleven halves.

183
00:12:58,466 --> 00:13:01,026
The left side is now x minus three,
squared.

184
00:13:02,166 --> 00:13:07,350
Take square roots: x equals three plus or
minus the square root of eleven halves,

185
00:13:07,350 --> 00:13:09,078
about two point three five.

186
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:15,743
The solutions are three plus or minus root
five point five, which are about five

187
00:13:15,743 --> 00:13:18,584
point three five and zero point six five.

188
00:13:19,733 --> 00:13:24,414
Watch out. Divide so the leading
coefficient is one before you start. Add

189
00:13:24,414 --> 00:13:29,544
half of b squared to both sides. And keep
the exact radical form if the question

190
00:13:29,544 --> 00:13:31,018
asks for exact answers.

191
00:13:32,166 --> 00:13:37,498
Your turn. Complete the square to solve x
squared plus eight x minus five equals

192
00:13:37,498 --> 00:13:39,697
zero. Pause the video and try it.

193
00:13:44,233 --> 00:13:49,638
Add five, then add sixteen: x plus four
squared equals twenty one. x equals

194
00:13:49,638 --> 00:13:52,809
negative four plus or minus root twenty
one.

195
00:13:53,933 --> 00:13:58,620
Completing the square on a general
quadratic gives a formula that solves

196
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:00,248
every quadratic equation.

197
00:14:01,366 --> 00:14:07,271
For a x squared plus b x plus c equals
zero, x equals negative b, plus or minus

198
00:14:07,271 --> 00:14:11,756
the square root of b squared minus four a
c, all over two a.

199
00:14:12,206 --> 00:14:13,507
It's worth memorizing.

200
00:14:14,633 --> 00:14:18,772
First, write the equation in standard
form, and read off a, b and c.

201
00:14:19,222 --> 00:14:25,065
For two x squared minus three x equals
two, subtract two: a is two, b is negative

202
00:14:25,065 --> 00:14:27,158
three, and c is negative two.

203
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:33,434
Plug in. b squared minus four a c is nine
plus sixteen, which is twenty-five, and

204
00:14:33,434 --> 00:14:34,956
its square root is five.

205
00:14:35,406 --> 00:14:41,016
So x equals three plus or minus five, over
four. That's two, or negative one half.

206
00:14:42,166 --> 00:14:44,257
The answers aren't always whole numbers.

207
00:14:44,707 --> 00:14:50,701
For x squared plus two x minus one equals
zero, x equals negative one plus or minus

208
00:14:50,701 --> 00:14:56,551
the square root of two. Leave it exact, or
round to about zero point four one and

209
00:14:56,551 --> 00:14:58,574
negative two point four one.

210
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:04,849
Which method to use? If there's no x term,
use square roots. If it factors easily,

211
00:15:04,849 --> 00:15:05,289
factor.

212
00:15:05,739 --> 00:15:09,174
Otherwise, use the quadratic formula. It
always works.

213
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:15,872
Your turn. Solve x squared minus four x
minus five equals zero with the quadratic

214
00:15:15,872 --> 00:15:16,422
formula.

215
00:15:16,872 --> 00:15:18,323
Pause the video and try it.

216
00:15:18,773 --> 00:15:25,169
b squared minus four a c is sixteen plus
twenty, which is thirty-six. x equals four

217
00:15:25,169 --> 00:15:29,098
plus or minus six, over two: five, or
negative one.

218
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:34,862
Here's a worked example of the quadratic
formula, with careful substitution.

219
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:41,590
Solve three x squared plus four x minus
two equals zero, rounding to the nearest

220
00:15:41,590 --> 00:15:42,252
hundredth.

221
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:49,202
Identify a equals three, b equals four,
and c equals negative two. Keep the signs.

222
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:56,110
Substitute into the formula: negative b
plus or minus the root of b squared minus

223
00:15:56,110 --> 00:15:57,608
four a c, over two a.

224
00:15:58,733 --> 00:16:04,237
Compute the discriminant first: sixteen
minus four times three times negative two,

225
00:16:04,237 --> 00:16:06,989
which is sixteen plus twenty four, forty.

226
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:12,592
So x equals negative four plus or minus
root forty, over six.

227
00:16:13,733 --> 00:16:16,037
Root forty is about six point three two.

228
00:16:17,166 --> 00:16:22,192
The plus gives about zero point three
nine, and the minus gives about negative

229
00:16:22,192 --> 00:16:23,481
one point seven two.

230
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:29,656
The solutions are about zero point three
nine and negative one point seven two.

231
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:35,984
Watch out. Put the equation in standard
form equal to zero first. Be careful with

232
00:16:35,984 --> 00:16:41,360
